# Scripts in scripts/ that nothing in the repository invokes, and why that is
# correct. Enforced in both directions by scripts/check-script-reachability.sh:
# an unreferenced script with no row here fails, and so does a row for a script
# that something now invokes, or a row naming a script that no longer exists.
#
# One row per (script, reason slug), with the finding above it. A row is a claim
# that this script is a tool a developer runs by hand, not a gate that was
# written and wired nowhere. The distinction matters: a gate nothing invokes
# reports nothing and is then cited as coverage, which is how
# scripts/test-zruntime.zig's script sat in the tree pointing at a root file
# that had been deleted.
#
# The list only ratchets down. Adding a row is a deliberate widening.

# Manual macOS experiment in dyld load overhead. Builds and times the binary;
# asserts nothing, so there is no verdict for a gate to consume.
build_minimal_dyld.sh manual-experiment

# Publishes the wasm analyzer into a separate website repository under a
# content-hashed filename. It writes outside this tree and needs that checkout,
# so it cannot run in CI. What CI does check is that the artifact still builds:
# `zig build wasm`, which scripts/verify.sh runs.
build-wasm-playground.sh publishes-outside-tree

# Two lines: build a TSX example ReleaseFast and serve it on port 3000. A
# convenience for looking at the JSX frontend by hand; it blocks on a server, so
# nothing automated can wait on it.
run-jsx.sh interactive-server

# Developer machine setup. Runs before the tree can be built at all, so no build
# step or gate could depend on it.
setup.sh developer-setup

# Spends real model time on three complete expert cohorts and prints a decision
# report. Report-only by design - it promotes no cassettes and edits no default -
# so there is no artifact for a gate to check, and running it automatically
# would spend on every build. docs/internals/cassette-recording.md is where the
# command is written down.
qualify-expert.sh manual-model-spend

# Regenerates docs/restrictions-to-proofs.md from restriction_registry.zig. The
# drift between the two is already gated - check-docs-drift.sh compares the
# rendered table against the registry row by row - so this script is the
# author-side fix for a failure that gate reports, not a check of its own.
update-restrictions-doc.sh regeneration-tool
